    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0578" n="462" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg462"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/1085.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Blanchard to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 20, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Consul at Gonaives reports that Saint Michel, Ennery, Limbe, Plaisance and other
                    surrounding places have taken up arms against the Government. It is reported
                    that Vilbrun Guillaume has proclaimed himself chief of the disaffections at Cape
                    Haitien.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
